n></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1192"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Jaffa (1192)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1192</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Jaffa of 1192 was the agreement that ended the Third Crusade, concluded between Saladin and Richard I of England.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1229"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Jaffa (1229)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1229</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Jaffa of 1229 was an agreement between the Ayyubid sultan al-Kamil and the Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II, by which Jerusalem was handed over to…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jeddah-1927"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-jeddah-1927.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Jeddah (1927)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1927</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Jeddah, signed on 20 May 1927 between Britain and Ibn Saud, recognised the full independence of his Kingdom of Hejaz and Nejd and its dependencies…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jeddah-2000"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-jeddah-2000.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Jeddah (2000)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 2000</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Jeddah, signed on 12 June 2000, settled the land and sea border between Saudi Arabia and Yemen, ending a dispute dating back to their war of 1934 and the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kadesh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-kadesh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Kadesh</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1258 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Kadesh, also known as the Egyptian–Hittite peace treaty, was concluded in 1258 BCE between Ramesses II of Egypt and the Hittite king Hattusili III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kalisz-1343"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-kalisz-1343.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Kalisz (1343)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1343</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Kalisz, concluded in July 1343, ended a long conflict between King Casimir III of Poland and the Teutonic Order.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kalisz-1813"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Kalisz (1813)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1813</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Kalisz (Kalisch) was signed on 28 February 1813 between Russia and Prussia after Napoleon's disastrous retreat from Moscow.</span></a></li></ul>
